From 2b8ec1507c7c354a4b7e8aee8cd2e971f07f40da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:04:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] feat(permissions): answer a node as LuckPerms answered it
 on Bukkit

The live server asks LuckPerms every Boolean node of the PermissionAPI
of Forge for an online player, through Arclight and hasPermission of
Bukkit, and the port must give the same answers until the owner rules
on issue #105. golem-permissions answers a node that no rule names as
undefined, and it refuses a node in upper case, so a caller would have
to know the rules of LuckPerms to answer as it did.

Permissions::has_permission keeps them in the port: it lowercases the
node as the calculator of LuckPerms does, answers a node that a rule
names by that rule and a node that nothing names with true for an
operator and false for every other player, as the processor of
LuckPerms for operators does. It allocates nothing for a node in lower
case, so the handler of the PermissionAPI may call it on any thread.

Link: https://github.com/skytekx/golem/issues/105
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016dYAZEa3eZnoeGd1c8FkBT
Signed-off-by: Florian Kleber <opensource@skytekx.com>
